Message-ID: <TqM6GEzXOmk.4qI79Rp4DAAJ@rqtl2-disc.groups.google.com>
In-Reply-To: <TqM6GEzXOmk.j6sV3yu9BQAJ@rqtl2-disc.groups.google.com>
References: <TqM6GEzXOmk.j6sV3yu9BQAJ@rqtl2-disc.groups.google.com>
Archived-At: <https://groups.google.com/g/rqtl2-disc/c/TqM6GEzXOmk/m/4qI79Rp4DAAJ>
MIME-Version: 1.0
Content-Type: text/plain; charset="utf-8"
Content-Transfer-Encoding: 8bit

The SNP association analysis that we do in the DO doesn't really apply for an F2 between two inbred strains, as there's no collapsing of multiple alleles that needs to occur. The results you get from scan1() are basically everything.

In plot_scan1, you could use type="p" or type="b" to have points plotted, if you want to see the LOD scores at individual markers.

karl

